# Walkthrough — Full Backend & Frontend Auth Integration

## What Was Built (Backend)
- **12 SQLite tables** with 7 seeded accounts
- **9 Express route modules** covering all 34 use cases ([auth](file:///d:/AG%20Projects/server/middleware/auth.js#5-21), `users`, `partners`, `groups`, `resources`, `messages`, `notifications`, `lostfound`, [admin](file:///d:/AG%20Projects/server/middleware/auth.js#22-29))
- **30/30 API tests passing**

## What Was Built (Frontend Phase 1)
- Added `server.proxy` to [vite.config.ts](file:///AG%20Projects/vite.config.ts) to forward `/api` requests to port 3001
- Created [src/api.ts](file:///d:/AG%20Projects/src/api.ts) to manage JWT tokens and wrap `fetch` calls
- Rewrote [LoginPage](file:///AG%20Projects/src/App.tsx#588-666) to hit `POST /api/auth/login`
- Rewrote [RegisterPage](file:///AG%20Projects/src/App.tsx#667-774) to hit `POST /api/auth/register`
- Rewrote [VerifyStudentPage](file:///AG%20Projects/src/App.tsx#775-822) to hit `POST /api/auth/verify`
- Rewrote [ResetPasswordPage](file:///AG%20Projects/src/App.tsx#823-878) to hit `POST /api/auth/reset-password`
- Handled global state mapping in [App.tsx](file:///AG%20Projects/src/App.tsx) from real API response

## Status
- **Backend:** Running on `http://localhost:3001`
- **Frontend App:** Running on `http://localhost:5173`

You can now open your browser and try logging in or registering a new account. It is communicating with the real database!

